- output height equals input height;
- every output row has the original width;
- every cell is an integer in the allowed palette/range;
- untouched cells exactly match the input;
- the changed-cell coordinates and replacement colors are precisely those predicted by a rule tested against all demos.

After incorrect feedback, review the exact submitted output against the source grid first. Distinguish malformed-grid errors from valid-but-wrong-rule errors. Then revise the hypothesis using the complete demo ledger; do not burn the remaining attempt budget on minor variations of an unsupported guess. If the rule is still underdetermined after the demo budget is exhausted, do not claim confidence or infer transformations merely from a visual regularity in the test.
